{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-007", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.25, "keywords": ["improve", "loss"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Triple-junction all-perovskite solar cell based on graphene oxide bilayer achieves 27.3% efficiency", "content": "<p>An international research team developed a triple-junction all-perovskite solar cell using a graphene oxide (GO)/self-assembled monolayer (SAM) bilayer contact strategy to overcome SAM-related charge extraction losses and improve interface quality.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/triple-junction-all-perovskite-solar-cell-based-on-graphene-oxide-bilayer-achieves-27-3-efficiency/\">Triple-junction all-perovskite solar cell based on graphene oxide bilayer achieves ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/triple-junction-all-perovskite-solar-cell-based-on-graphene-oxide-bilayer-achieves-27-3-efficiency/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-008", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "France’s Reden halts solar module production", "content": "<p>Reden has halted solar module production at its Roquefort-sur-Soulzon facility, citing mounting cost pressures and competition from Asian manufacturers. The closure marks another setback for French solar manufacturing, leaving Voltec as the country’s only remaining PV panel producer.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/frances-reden-halts-solar-module-production/\">France&#8217;s Reden halts solar module production</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magaz", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/frances-reden-halts-solar-module-production/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-009", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "KUKA Cable highlights material innovation as the next frontier of solar cable reliability", "content": "<p>As Europe’s solar market continues to expand, long-term cable reliability is becoming a critical factor in project safety and performance. At The smarter E Europe 2026 in Munich, KUKA Cable highlighted the growing importance of material innovation and systematic quality verification in meeting the demands of next-generation solar projects.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/kuka-cable-highlights-material-innovation-as-the-next-frontier-of-solar-cable-reliability/\"", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/kuka-cable-highlights-material-innovation-as-the-next-frontier-of-solar-cable-reliability/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-010", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Türkiye to tender 900 MW of solar", "content": "<p>The forthcoming round of Türkiye’s renewable energy tenders for solar and wind will open on October 13, including 14 solar projects with a combined capacity of 900 MW. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/turkiye-to-tender-900-mw-of-solar/\">Türkiye to tender 900 MW of solar</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/turkiye-to-tender-900-mw-of-solar/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-011", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Germany energy provider builds 50 MW power-to-heat system", "content": "<p>Enercity is building a 50 MW power-to-heat plant in Hanover to support its coal phase-out, decarbonize district heating, and absorb surplus renewable electricity. The facility will expand the utility’s flexibility by converting excess power into heat for the district heating network and storage systems.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/germany-energy-provider-builds-50-mw-power-to-heat-system/\">Germany energy provider builds 50 MW power-to-heat system</a> appear", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/germany-energy-provider-builds-50-mw-power-to-heat-system/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-012", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Daikin unveils inverter-driven rooftop heat pump for light commercial buildings", "content": "<p>Daikin has unveiled an inverter-driven rooftop heat pump offering 7.5-ton to 10-ton capacities. The system uses difluoromethane refrigerant and reportedly achieves a coefficient of performance of up to 3.85 at 8.3 C</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/daikin-unveils-inverter-driven-rooftop-heat-pump-for-light-commercial-buildings/\">Daikin unveils inverter-driven rooftop heat pump for light commercial buildings</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/daikin-unveils-inverter-driven-rooftop-heat-pump-for-light-commercial-buildings/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-013", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "‘Australian first’ compressed CO2 battery project takes shape", "content": "<p>The Victorian government and Italian clean technology company Energy Dome have announced plans to develop Australia’s first long-duration compressed carbon dioxide battery energy storage facility in the heart of the state's coal country.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/sec-plans-australian-first-compressed-co2-battery-in-victorian-coal-country/\">‘Australian first’ compressed CO2 battery project takes shape</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/sec-plans-australian-first-compressed-co2-battery-in-victorian-coal-country/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-13-014", "date": "2026-07-13", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Mon"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Spain targets wafer production", "content": "<p>Spain-based Sunwafe is planning a 20 GW ingot and wafer factory. The project is progressing quickly, with a site secured in northern Spain and a €200 million ($232.6 million) grant, newly appointed CEO Michael Pinto tells pv magazine. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/spain-targets-wafer-production/\">Spain targets wafer production</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/13/spain-targets-wafer-production/", "type": "rss"}]}
